#
# Declarative example-conformance fixtures for the concepts slice — the test-DSL
# twin of the SHACL pytest in tests/test_concepts.py ("this instance must
# validate, that counter-example must be rejected"). The harness
# (crates/slicetest run_conformance_cell) validates concepts/module.ttl + the one
# bound gmeow:exampleFile against concepts/shapes.ttl and compares finding codes.
#
# MESSAGE→CODE shift: the original pytest asserted a specific sh:message substring;
# these cells pin the constraint-component CODE (shacl.<ConstraintComponentLocalName>,
# from gmeow_validate::findings::finding_from_shacl). This is the same lossy shift
# the epistemics exemplar accepted: the code form COLLAPSES distinct sh:message
# strings that share a constraint component — e.g. a missing-feature and a
# missing-interval both report shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent, indistinguishable
# by code alone. Because each counter-example is a SEPARATE fixture isolating ONE
# violation, the (fixture, code) pair still pins the specific constraint faithfully.
#
# CODE VERIFICATION. Every expectedViolationCode below is pinned to the sh:sourceShape
# it must come from (gmeow:expectedSourceShape), which the harness enforces — a fixture
# that reds a DIFFERENT rule of the same component no longer passes.
#
# WHY NO CELL DECLARES gmeow:expectedSoleFinding. These cells used to claim "and NO other
# finding". Measured against the harness, all four are false, and for one structural
# reason: this slice has not finished migrating, so it still ships a residual
# hand-authored shapes.ttl (gmeow:ConceptCategorizationShape, gmeow:ConceptTenureShape)
# ALONGSIDE the derived gmeow:ConceptCategorization-shape / gmeow:ConceptTenure-shape the
# pipeline projects from the same module axioms. One defect is therefore reported TWICE,
# by two sh:sourceShapes — which is what soleness measures, and it counts two authorities
# as two even when they say the same thing. The duplication is the defect, not the
# fixtures: soleness becomes declarable here the moment the residual shapes.ttl is retired
# and the derived surface is the only authority.
#
# The two CONFORMING fixtures live under tests/conformance-fixtures/ (NOT
# examples/) and the four counter-examples under tests/counter-examples/, so the
# global `make validate` gate never loads them as data; they are therefore
# validated SLICE-SCOPED only (module + slice shapes), intentional and mirroring
# the epistemics flagship-exclusion rationale.
#
# See dsl/tests/MIGRATION-LEDGER.md for the per-test pytest→DSL mapping.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/concepts/tests/> .

# --- Conforming: a well-formed ConceptCategorization ------------------------
ex:ecCategorizationConforms a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/categorization-wellformed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The fixture supplies exactly one gmeow:observedFeature (a gmeow:Entity), one gmeow:observationResult (a gmeow:Concept), a gmeow:observationMethod, and an in-range gmeow:typicality, so it satisfies gmeow:ConceptCategorizationShape and validates with no findings. Mirrors test_wellformed_concept_categorization_conforms." .

# --- Conforming: a well-formed ConceptTenure --------------------------------
ex:ecTenureConforms a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/tenure-wellformed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The fixture supplies exactly one gmeow:conceptHoldsFor (a gmeow:Concept) and one gmeow:duringInterval (a gmeow:TimeInterval), so it satisfies gmeow:ConceptTenureShape and validates with no findings. Mirrors test_wellformed_concept_tenure_conforms." .

# --- Violating: ConceptCategorization missing observedFeature ----------------
ex:ecCategorizationMissingFeature a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/categorization-missing-feature.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape gmeow:ConceptCategorizationShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example omits gmeow:observedFeature (sh:minCount 1 on gmeow:ConceptCategorizationShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent from gmeow:ConceptCategorizationShape, which gmeow:expectedSourceShape pins by IRI. The derived gmeow:ConceptCategorization-shape reports the SAME missing member as shacl.QualifiedMinCountConstraintComponent, so the cell cannot declare gmeow:expectedSoleFinding while the residual shapes.ttl duplicates the derived authority (see the header note). Mirrors test_categorization_missing_feature_is_flagged." .

# --- Violating: observationResult is not a Concept ---------------------------
ex:ecCategorizationResultNotConcept a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/categorization-result-not-concept.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.ClassConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape gmeow:ConceptCategorization-shape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example's gmeow:observationResult (ex:vehicle) is a gmeow:Entity but NOT a gmeow:Concept (sh:class gmeow:Concept), so validation MUST emit shacl.ClassConstraintComponent from gmeow:ConceptCategorization-shape, which gmeow:expectedSourceShape pins by IRI. The residual gmeow:ConceptCategorizationShape reports the same class violation a second time, and the derived shape additionally reports shacl.QualifiedMinCountConstraintComponent because a non-Concept value cannot satisfy the qualified result restriction; the cell therefore does not declare gmeow:expectedSoleFinding (see the header note). Mirrors test_categorization_result_not_concept_is_flagged." .

# --- Violating: typicality out of the closed interval [0,1] ------------------
ex:ecCategorizationTypicalityOutOfRange a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/categorization-typicality-out-of-range.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MaxInclusiveConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape gmeow:ConceptCategorization-shape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example's gmeow:typicality is 1.5, above sh:maxInclusive 1 (sh:minInclusive 0 and sh:datatype xsd:decimal are both satisfied), so validation MUST emit shacl.MaxInclusiveConstraintComponent from gmeow:ConceptCategorization-shape, which gmeow:expectedSourceShape pins by IRI. The residual gmeow:ConceptCategorizationShape reports the identical range violation a second time, so the cell does not declare gmeow:expectedSoleFinding (see the header note). Mirrors test_categorization_typicality_out_of_range_is_flagged." .

# --- Violating: ConceptTenure missing duringInterval -------------------------
ex:ecTenureMissingInterval a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/tenure-missing-interval.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape gmeow:ConceptTenureShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example omits gmeow:duringInterval (sh:minCount 1 on gmeow:ConceptTenureShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent from gmeow:ConceptTenureShape, which gmeow:expectedSourceShape pins by IRI. The derived gmeow:ConceptTenure-shape reports the SAME missing interval as shacl.QualifiedMinCountConstraintComponent, so the cell does not declare gmeow:expectedSoleFinding (see the header note). Mirrors test_tenure_missing_interval_is_flagged." .
